hello and welcome to Playstation grenade  I decided to pick up little nightmares  over the weekend I needed a break from  my other horror titles but I wanted  something that was eerie and still had  elements of horror  I enjoyed these few hours witless  madness so much that I wanted to tell  you eight reason why little nightmares  deserves a spot in your game collection  to get you in the right mindset I'm  going to start off by comparing little  nightmares with other games that you may  have played in the past if you've ever  played the two masterpieces limbo or  inside then you know what to expect here  not only those little nightmares use a  very similar control system and puzzle  platformer elements it also has a very  similar take on ambiguous narrative and  storytelling and showing things in a  visual way wherever possible  let's look at the aesthetic in the  setting first little nightmares please  view in the shoes or lack of shoes of  six a tiny yellow raincoat wearing child  give a no backstory or understanding of  where she is or what she should do next  you have a tiny lighter to illuminate  the nooks and crannies you tentatively  wonder through but it isn't quite enough  to fully assess your next step  keeping you on edge in where's your  scare horror just can't compete with the  environment you pass through is  deliberately oversized adding to the  wonderment of being a child in  unfamiliar surroundings it isn't a  well-kept world its rundown its  rat-infested and you're witness of  shocking sight taking center stage you  will see a pair of legs above a chair  with a letter close by but you are not  given any more information you are  forced to paint your own picture as he  committed suicide did he leave a note I  even tried to pick up the letter as I  was so engrossed in the deliberate lack  of explanation at any in every step of  this game the story is deliberately  vague throughout and you'll be  scratching your head about what the  narrative could be even after finishing  the game you'll be unsure what just  happened  the desire to escape the hostile  environment is the fixation the game  implanting you early on and the more the  ocean facility you awaken has many  levels to progress through with  different distinct visuals  in the early parts of the game you are  seemingly in the prison and a kitchen  six is regularly overpowered by hunger  pins and you are forced to try out new  cuisine in order to continue your  journey in terms of mechanical nightmare  is a slick platformer with small puddles  thrown in regularly although it's  effectively a side scroll the  verticality of each environment is  breathtaking  I find myself checking how deep the  chasm was by pushing objects into the  void and waiting for the impact on the  ground below duty our diminutive stature  pressing buttons can be difficult and  requires thought even listening a small  key can cause issues for 6 which leads  me into the real mechanic of this game  hide-and-seek  [Music]  I know it sounds childish and that's  exactly how we should feel hiding under  a table in the hooks your enemy will  walk past is enough to make you hold  your breath running too fast will also  alert enemies meaning creeping slowly is  sometimes with a greater option but  feels like a lifetime of torment for  your heart the enemies you encounter are  a marvel of artistry and unique action  from the leeches that can smother you in  a split second to the janitor who can  reach you from seemingly miles away the  nuances each encounter offer are  spectacular the boss fights that follow  although brief are enough to keep you  thinking about the game days later in a  world where games are expected to last  20 plus hours and offer robust online  support little nightmares dares to be  different this is a single story with no  additional roots to uncover or hidden  items to unlock it does approach  collectables with little norm characters  locate and dole figurines to smash in  order to unlock concept art for the  campaign well it lasted me about three  hours I have spoken to other people  who've taken up to eight hours to  progress through the story and others  suggest about five hours is the typical  length to get through this game at this  point I can't decide if the short length  is a positive or a criticism but one  thing is for certain I want to play more  and not many games make me feel that way  the game's length is reflected in the  price of the product here in the UK it  retails around 16 pounds and in the US  it's only $20 so around a third of the  price of a typical video game only you  can decide if you think it's worth it I  wanted to finish off by assuring you  that this is completely my own opinion  I bought little nightmares from my own  wallet I wasn't asked to review it I  wasn't paid to do this PlayStation  granade is independent and we are very  proud to be so have you tried little  nightmares and what do you think to it  oh what the heck is the story about  please post your opinions below but put  a spoiler tag on anything to do with the  story  I am Adam from PlayStation granade I've  seen  time
 

